{"name":"Orange Lily","hex":"#be7249","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"orange lily","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Lilium bulbiferum, a herbaceous European lily with underground bulbs and orange flowers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange_lily"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lilium bulbiferum","blocks":[{"text":"Lilium bulbiferum, common names orange lily, fire lily, Jimmy's Bane, tiger lily and St. John's Lily, is a herbaceous European lily with underground bulbs, belonging to the Liliaceae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Lilium_bulbiferum_var._bulbiferum_01.JPG/330px-Lilium_bulbiferum_var._bulbiferum_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lilium_bulbiferum","wikidata":"Q163766"},{"title":"Lilium","blocks":[{"text":"Lilium is a genus of herbaceous flowering plants growing from bulbs, all with large and often prominent flowers. Lilies are a group of flowering plants which are important in culture and literature in much of the world. Most species are native to the Northern Hemisphere and their range is temperate climates and extends into the subtropics. Many other plants have \"lily\" in their common names, but do not belong to the same genus and are therefore not true lilies. True lilies are known to be highly toxic to cats."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Lilium_candidum_1.jpg/330px-Lilium_candidum_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lilium","wikidata":"Q5194627"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(colour)","wikidata":"Q39338"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Orange_Lily_-_Lilium_bulbiferum_in_Manali_%285%29.jpg/500px-Orange_Lily_-_Lilium_bulbiferum_in_Manali_%285%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Orange_Lily_-_Lilium_bulbiferum_in_Manali_%285%29.jpg/1280px-Orange_Lily_-_Lilium_bulbiferum_in_Manali_%285%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Orange_Lily_-_Lilium_bulbiferum_in_Manali_%285%29.jpg/500px-Orange_Lily_-_Lilium_bulbiferum_in_Manali_%285%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flower and flower buds","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOrange_Lily_-_Lilium_bulbiferum_in_Manali_(5).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Lillium_Stamens.jpg/500px-Lillium_Stamens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Lillium_Stamens.jpg/1280px-Lillium_Stamens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Lillium_Stamens.jpg/500px-Lillium_Stamens.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lilium longiflorum flower – 1. stigma, 2. style, 3. anthers, 4. filament, 5. tepal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALillium_Stamens.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikip